@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #91AED1
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #4A302B
skinparam noteBorderColor #F1AD8A
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title Constraint application — common rules and accepted core
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Common contract interpretation\nCurrent scoped authority + attributable result\nFrame and operation-specific reconciliation" as common
rectangle "DC-O01 — Edit source only\nDC-I01: scoped identity\nDC-I02: source-edit independence\nDC-I04: actual-history independence" as o1
rectangle "DC-O02 — Apply selected changes\nDC-I02: independent tailoring\nDC-I03: separate publication\nDC-I04: actual-history independence" as o2
rectangle "DC-O03 — Publish separately\nDC-I03: separate publication\nDC-I04: actual-history independence\nDC-I06: distinct representation facts" as o3
common ..> o1 : constrains
common ..> o2 : constrains
common ..> o3 : constrains
legend bottom
Selected constraint-to-operation graph; arrows mean applicability, not execution order.
The complete 18-constraint reverse index is in file 10. No logical implication or full test coverage is claimed.
endlegend

@enduml
